<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Adolf Friedrich of Mecklenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1873">1873</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf Friedrich of Mecklenburg was a German prince, explorer and colonial governor. He led a scientific expedition across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 1907–1908 and was governor of German Togoland from 1912 to 1914. In November 1918 Baltic German leaders chose him as head of the planned United Baltic Duchy, but the state collapsed before he could take office. He later served as president of the German Olympic Committee.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duke-adolf-friedrich-of-mecklenburg.jpg" alt="Duke Adolf Friedrich of Mecklenburg" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolf_Friedrich_of_Mecklenburg_(vor_1910).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
